\h Isaiah
\c 40
\s1 Prepare the Way for the LORD
\r (\ref Matthew 3:1–12|MAT 3:1-12\ref*; \ref Mark 1:1–8|MRK 1:1-8\ref*; \ref Luke 3:1–20|LUK 3:1-20\ref*; \ref John 1:19–28|JHN 1:19-28\ref*)
\q1 \v 1 “Comfort, comfort My people,”
\q2 says your God.
\q1 \v 2 “Speak tenderly to Jerusalem,
\q2 and proclaim to her
\q1 that her forced labor has been completed;
\q2 her iniquity has been pardoned.
\q1 For she has received from the hand of the LORD
\q2 double for all her sins.”
\p \v 3 A voice of one calling:
\b 
\q1 “Prepare the way for the LORD in the wilderness;\f + \fr 40:3 \ft Or \fqa A voice of one calling in the wilderness: “Prepare the way for the LORD\f*
\q2 make a straight highway for our God in the desert.\f + \fr 40:3 \ft LXX \fqa make straight the paths of our God\ft ; cited in \ref Matthew 3:3|MAT 3:3\ref*, Mark 1:3, Luke 3:4, and John 1:23\f*
\q1 \v 4 Every valley shall be lifted up,
\q2 and every mountain and hill made low;
\q1 the uneven ground will become smooth,
\q2 and the rugged land a plain.\f + \fr 40:4 \ft LXX \fqa Every valley shall be filled in, and every mountain and hill shall be brought low. All the crooked ways shall become straight, and the rough places plains.\ft Cited in \ref Luke 3:5|LUK 3:5\ref*\f*
\q1 \v 5 And the glory of the LORD will be revealed,
\q2 and all humanity together will see it.”\f + \fr 40:5 \ft Literally \fqa and all flesh together will see it.\ft Cited in \ref Luke 3:6|LUK 3:6\ref*\f*
\qr For the mouth of the LORD has spoken.
